//
// Expected: c1c0 at one session and at two.
//
// The entry swaps Alice's two keys. Substitution is simultaneous, so `x` is
// sealed under `t2`, which Bob leaks, and `y` under `t1`, which nobody does:
// the verdicts are those of the model as written, exchanged. Each target is
// also the other's value, so Alice still holds both. Dropping every rebound
// target from her `knows` once left her using `t2` without declaring it,
// and the model was rejected with "unknown constant `t2`".
//
// scenario_binding_chain.vp is the counterweight: `t1 = t2, t2 = t3` gives
// c0c1, since `t1` becomes `t2` and stops there.

attacker[passive]

principal Alice[
	knows private t1, t2
	generates n1, n2
	x = ENC(t1, n1)
	y = ENC(t2, n2)
]

Alice -> Bob: x, y

principal Bob[
	knows private t2
	leaks t2
]

scenarios[
	Alice[t1 = t2, t2 = t1]
]

queries[
	confidentiality? n1
	confidentiality? n2
]
